# Project Workflow Rules

Before installing, removing, or updating dependencies in `package.json`, you MUST run `nvm use` first in the same shell session.

Dependency-management commands are forbidden until this preflight is done:

1. Run `nvm use`
2. Run `node -v` and ensure the active version matches the project requirement from `package.json`

This applies to commands like `npm install`, `npm add`, `npm remove`, `npm update`, `npm ci`, and any other workflow that changes project packages.

If `nvm use` was not run first, STOP and run it before continuing.
